{"duration_api_ms":119617,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d91ea047-ef0c-4a09-9a14-b5c5096f5861","total_cost_usd":0.811793,"usage":{"input_tokens":30,"cache_creation_input_tokens":48935,"cache_read_input_tokens":985165,"output_tokens":11158,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":754},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":48935,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1246,"cache_read_input_tokens":80907,"cache_creation_input_tokens":366,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":366},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":30,"outputTokens":11158,"cacheReadInputTokens":985165,"cacheCreationInputTokens":48935,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.811793,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":754,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":48935,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":15,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the AUD-7 audit, two proposals (TEP-0016, TEP-0017) and two follow-up requests, and committed them on the packet branch. Both acceptance commands pass and `theseus scope-check` is ok. `theseus validate` reports one error: the `layout-finish-webapps` stage of journey `open-docx-100p` is not covered in `DIAG-web-apps-documenteditor.md`. My changes don't touch journey or diagnosis files, so it should have been there before, though I didn't run validate on a clean checkout to confirm. It's outside my target, so I left it.\n\n**What the audit covers:** records 140–164, which is 25 records for 23 packets: 21 done, 3 blocked, 1 discarded.\n\n**Main numbers:**\n- **Approval on first review:** the scoreboard says 81%, but the real figure is 67%. PKT-0109, 0137 and 0149 failed an acceptance command and are still marked as approved on first review.\n- **Blocked cost:** at most 14% of spend, down from 60% in AUD-6.\n- **Median time for a done packet:** 8.9 minutes, down from 15.6.\n- **Review cost:** 20% of done-packet cost. All 5 rejections that weren't acceptance failures were correct and specific.\n- **Planner estimates:** they exist on only 7 of 25 records. On those, the line estimates are good, but the file counts are too low on all 7.\n\n**Proposals under test:**\n- **TEP-0011 (scope-check):** confirmed. Only one out-of-target rejection in 25 records.\n- **TEP-0012 (new packet types):** confirmed for `measure` (75% approved on first review). No `chore` packet ran, and 2 friction lines still say a type was missing.\n- **TEP-0013 (journeys):** the 10-page open is at 3662 ms against a 2.5 s target, so that half is not met yet.\n- **TEP-0001 (stop on an external blocker):** confirmed, but PKT-0132 still used 4 attempts before it stopped on a speed-up too small to measure.\n\n**New proposals:**\n- **TEP-0016:** mark a record approved on first review only if nothing rejected it, drop the `out_of_context_reads` field (empty on every record for seven audits), and have the planner count packet, friction and spawn files in its file estimate.\n- **TEP-0017:** when the differential test fails, it names each check that differed and reruns those once. A pass on rerun sets `flaky_oracle: true`. Today that field is never true, while 0109 and 0149 were rejected on differences that didn't reproduce.\n\n**Follow-ups requested:** a shared helper for the journey test scripts, which have been copied four times. And a note in `environment.md` on where the `external/` repository mirrors are, since PKT-0137 and PKT-0138 found `external/` empty in their worktree.\n\n**Decisions:**\n- I reported approval both ways, as recorded and as corrected.\n- I treated blocked cost as an upper bound because PKT-0132's cost entries look cumulative.\n- I audited as claude-opus-5-5, the same model family that ran and reviewed every packet in the period, because no other family was available. This is recorded as F3.\n\n**Lessons for the Atlas:**\n- `theseus packet new --help` lists only 7 packet types, though the command accepts `chore` and `measure`.\n- PKT-0133's record says 1 attempt while its block reason says 3.\n- `journeys.jsonl` now exists, so journey timings can be read straight from the scoreboard.\n\nAll of this is in the packet's Executor log and in my friction line.","ttft_ms":3854,"type":"result","duration_ms":127011,"uuid":"e26e3ffb-c758-43a0-b528-c849a64028ad","ttft_stream_ms":2825,"time_to_request_ms":258,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":4,"system_prompt":160,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":15,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":5,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":0,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"request_announcements":10,"query_setup":2,"auto_mode_context_wait":7,"model_gates":1,"tool_schema_build":14,"message_normalization":2,"client_creation":8,"request_build":11},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":43,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":125,"time_to_request_major_faults":23,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":209,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":137,"process_rss_mib_result":232,"process_anon_mib_result":143,"process_peak_rss_mib":243,"process_cpu_ms_turn":2860,"process_wall_ms_turn":12701